    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node versions disagree: ^24.0.0 (package.json engines.node), 20 (.nvmrc), 24 (release.yml).",
        "  20 (.nvmrc) lies outside engines.node ^24.0.0.",
        "  The release is built on one of them and a contributor may build on another; a different major gets a different lockfile and, with a native dependency, a different build."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "resources/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Controller/PageController.php:169 reaches it through dirname(__DIR__, 2).",
        "tests/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Command/SeedTestLibraryCommand.php:97 reaches it through dirname(__DIR__, 2).",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set, so the tarball lacks them and the app fails in the code that reads them, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += resources tests ships them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is sheetmusic, the checkout directory is nextcloud-sheetmusic.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "link-redirect",
      "lines": [
        "A link of appinfo/info.xml has moved permanently:",
        "  <donation> https://www.paypal.me/cpwick",
        "    now https://www.paypal.com/paypalme/cpwick",
        "  The old address works only as long as the redirect is kept; the new one can be stated directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 31 to 36; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 31 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.js), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "2 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/stylelint-config, opentype.js.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 764 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL-3.0-or-later (appinfo/info.xml, package.json, composer.json).",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
      "lines": [
        "Version 0.1.0 in appinfo/info.xml, package.json and package-lock.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
